        "original_id": "8db6340a-6c61-56ac-94e8-918777f3211b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bob Johnson\n- Organizations: Derry City F.C., Barnsley\n- Places: Ireland, Northern Ireland\n- Topics: Non-league football, Irish League\n\nFacts:\n- Derry City F.C. was founded in 1928.\n- Derry City F.C. initially played in the Irish League, the domestic league in Northern Ireland.\n- Bob Johnson played in Ireland for Derry City.\n- Bob Johnson was on the books of Barnsley but did not play for the club in the League.\n- Bob Johnson played non-league football for Ushaw Moor, Moor Ends Thorne, Firbeck Colliery, Spennymoor United, Thorne Colliery, Eden Colliery, and Walker Celtic.\n- Derry City F.C. won the Irish League title in 1964–65.",
